1
00:00:42,399 --> 00:00:44,619
Off to meet up with that Shanghai girl, huh?

2
00:00:45,159 --> 00:00:48,140
What? We're just shopping for New Year's.

3
00:00:49,659 --> 00:00:51,280
Decked out like a bourgeois.

4
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:52,320
Looking sketchy as hell.

5
00:00:53,619 --> 00:00:55,240
This is called denim.

6
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:57,079
It's stylish, you know?

7
00:00:58,380 --> 00:00:59,759
Stylish, my foot.

8
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:02,560
It's the same color as a thermos. Seriously.

9
00:01:06,239 --> 00:01:07,019
You don't know a thing.

10
00:01:08,019 --> 00:01:08,739
It looks so good!

11
00:01:29,219 --> 00:01:29,719
Haizhu.

12
00:01:43,219 --> 00:01:43,980
Off we go!

13
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:53,200
I told you I should've brought another bike.

14
00:01:53,319 --> 00:01:54,939
Where do we put the New Year's goods?

15
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:55,700
On the back rack.

16
00:01:56,319 --> 00:01:58,159
I brought a hemp rope. They'll be tied down tight.

17
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:01,280
If the back is loaded up, where do I sit?

18
00:02:02,239 --> 00:02:03,260
I forgot about you.

19
00:02:05,239 --> 00:02:05,819
Just kidding.

20
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,480
You can sit on the crossbar.

21
00:02:07,579 --> 00:02:08,879
I ride steady. You won't feel a bump.

22
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:19,000
Tell me...

23
00:02:20,919 --> 00:02:23,120
If there's a chance to get a job back home,

24
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,379
should I go back to Shanghai?

25
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:29,020
You want to go back to Shanghai?

26
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:32,060
I'm asking you.

27
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:35,680
What's so great about Shanghai anyway?

28
00:02:39,819 --> 00:02:41,780
Shanghai's buildings are really tall.

29
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,740
My home is near the Huangpu River.

30
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:47,539
Open the window, and you see the water.

31
00:02:48,979 --> 00:02:49,740
And the weather...

32
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:51,199
is a lot warmer than here.

33
00:02:52,819 --> 00:02:54,699
No matter how tall Shanghai's buildings are,

34
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:56,860
can they be taller than our plant's chimneys?

35
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:59,599
It's just different from Songliao.

36
00:03:02,539 --> 00:03:03,680
Shanghai has tall buildings,

37
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,419
but Songliao will have them too.

38
00:03:05,879 --> 00:03:07,000
Shanghai has the Huangpu River,

39
00:03:07,199 --> 00:03:08,620
but our Songliao has the Song River.

40
00:03:12,719 --> 00:03:13,639
Shanghai's river...

41
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:15,180
never freezes in winter.

42
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:20,379
Does Shanghai even have any good food?

43
00:03:20,539 --> 00:03:21,840
I can learn to cook it for you.

44
00:03:22,439 --> 00:03:24,080
I... I can also make...

45
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:25,360
potato stew,

46
00:03:26,259 --> 00:03:27,000
s-sticky bean buns...

47
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:28,740
I can braise meat, too.

48
00:03:29,879 --> 00:03:31,039
A-And we have frozen pears!

49
00:03:31,199 --> 00:03:31,680
You know,

50
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:32,979
right? Sweet,

51
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:33,759
cool and refreshing.

52
00:03:34,379 --> 00:03:35,900
T-Taking a bite is just so good!

53
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:44,060
Songliao has things Shanghai doesn't.

54
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,300
Don't go back.

55
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:52,340
Stay here.

56
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:18,240
A huge dance hall like that,

57
00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:19,660
I left you in charge of it,

58
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,800
and you just let them trash the place?

59
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:22,980
What good are you?

60
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:26,139
My girls told me,

61
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:28,519
Eastern Tyrant's gang is running wild out there.

62
00:04:29,399 --> 00:04:30,519
They've even put the word out.

63
00:04:31,579 --> 00:04:32,279
His sights are set high.

64
00:04:32,699 --> 00:04:34,519
He's not just after the east side.

65
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:37,639
Songliao has two kings.

66
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,259
And as for you,

67
00:04:39,939 --> 00:04:40,879
you're slipping.

68
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:45,800
I'm talking to you!

69
00:04:46,399 --> 00:04:47,660
What the hell do I keep you around for?

70
00:04:47,839 --> 00:04:48,579
What use are you?

71
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:50,560
Brother,

72
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:52,519
this... this really wasn't my fault.

73
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:54,100
We just didn't have enough men.

74
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,259
Of course we took a beating.

75
00:04:56,439 --> 00:04:56,980
Someone like you?

76
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:58,220
Even a hundred men would be wasted on you.

77
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,759
Brother, there's another thing.

78
00:05:00,259 --> 00:05:01,040
Lately, Eastern Tyrant...

79
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,819
has been hanging around the shipyard gang.

80
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:05,160
That shipyard isn't ours.

81
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:06,360
What do you mean?

82
00:05:07,759 --> 00:05:08,759
Eastern Tyrant and Ma Limin...

83
00:05:08,839 --> 00:05:09,480
have been joined at the hip lately.

84
00:05:10,399 --> 00:05:11,480
I don't know about Ma Limin,

85
00:05:11,879 --> 00:05:13,819
but he's hanging with a worker named Liu Haizhu.

86
00:05:14,019 --> 00:05:14,839
Right, right, right.

87
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:16,699
This Liu Haizhu...

88
00:05:17,079 --> 00:05:18,459
is with Eastern Tyrant.

89
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:20,319
He's the one who led the raid on the dance hall!

90
00:05:20,839 --> 00:05:21,339
Brother,

91
00:05:21,959 --> 00:05:23,439
give me more men this time.

92
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:25,720
Just watch me beat him up good!

93
00:05:30,399 --> 00:05:31,579
If you ask me,

94
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:33,839
you ought to learn from Brother He.

95
00:05:34,639 --> 00:05:35,560
Back in the day, Brother He...

96
00:05:35,779 --> 00:05:37,019
was surrounded by a bunch of cops,

97
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:39,439
yet he walked right out like it was nothing.

98
00:05:41,139 --> 00:05:41,959
And looking at Songliao...

99
00:05:42,259 --> 00:05:42,740
in all these years,

100
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:44,500
has anyone ever beaten Brother He?

101
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:45,740
Not a single one.

102
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:47,180
And you guys?

103
00:05:49,459 --> 00:05:50,819
Say what's on your mind.

104
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:51,819
Don't beat around the bush.

105
00:05:53,399 --> 00:05:54,000
Brother,

106
00:05:55,519 --> 00:05:56,300
it's been five years.

107
00:05:57,459 --> 00:05:59,439
You came back after five years to wait for a chance.

108
00:05:59,779 --> 00:06:00,959
Not to prove you're great,

109
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,439
but to show people...

110
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:04,160
that what you lost, you will take back!

111
00:06:05,819 --> 00:06:06,860
And how do you take it back?

112
00:06:07,879 --> 00:06:09,180
You have to take Eastern Tyrant,

113
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:11,160
Liu Haizhu, and that whole bunch down.

114
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:12,639
That's how you'll run the turf.

115
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,240
You'll be the true boss!

116
00:06:23,439 --> 00:06:24,819
Trying to use me as a pawn?

117
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:28,120
Brother He.

118
00:06:28,459 --> 00:06:28,899
Brother He.

119
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,579
Didn't you tell Lao Ba earlier...

120
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:32,800
that you were looking for two guys?

121
00:06:47,959 --> 00:06:49,139
I've got something good here.

122
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:52,319
I never found the right chance to give it to you.

123
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,939
Take a look. Does he look familiar?

124
00:07:04,279 --> 00:07:05,839
This is his name right here.

125
00:07:06,139 --> 00:07:06,579
It reads...

126
00:07:06,939 --> 00:07:09,500
Liu Haizhu.

127
00:07:28,579 --> 00:07:29,040
Hello.

128
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:29,800
Hello.

129
00:07:38,939 --> 00:07:39,519
Haizhu.

130
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:42,980
I notice you always wear that same sweater.

131
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,980
Let me knit you a new one.

132
00:07:47,839 --> 00:07:49,279
You know how to knit?

133
00:07:50,759 --> 00:07:51,680
There's plenty I know how to do.

134
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:53,680
No need.

135
00:07:53,779 --> 00:07:55,019
This one's still holding up fine.

136
00:07:55,339 --> 00:07:55,879
It's fine.

137
00:07:59,459 --> 00:08:00,439
This color is nice.

138
00:08:00,779 --> 00:08:01,680
It's festive for the New Year.

139
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:06,860
Isn't this a girl's color?

140
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:10,620
Wearing this lets people know someone's thinking of you.

141
00:08:11,959 --> 00:08:12,740
How much is this?

142
00:08:12,879 --> 00:08:13,620
Two-fifty a liang.

143
00:08:14,079 --> 00:08:14,939
Weigh out a jin for me, please.

144
00:08:15,079 --> 00:08:15,819
Sure, I'll get it for you.

145
00:08:15,839 --> 00:08:16,279
Thanks.

146
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:16,920
You're welcome.

147
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:22,379
Excuse me, comrade.

148
00:08:22,519 --> 00:08:24,100
Could you hand me that, uh...

149
00:08:24,199 --> 00:08:26,259
that mauve scarf over there?

150
00:08:27,259 --> 00:08:27,839
This looks really nice.

151
00:08:27,959 --> 00:08:28,360
Thanks.

152
00:08:28,459 --> 00:08:29,079
You're welcome.

153
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:30,639
Is this picked out for me?

154
00:08:32,419 --> 00:08:33,360
Even the clerk said it looks nice.

155
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:34,220
Try it on. Come on.

156
00:08:35,679 --> 00:08:36,120
This...

157
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:40,899
Can this really look good?

158
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:41,580
It looks great.

159
00:08:42,639 --> 00:08:43,320
It really does.

160
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:45,759
Excuse me,

161
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:47,120
could I borrow your mirror?

162
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:48,779
See?

163
00:08:52,299 --> 00:08:53,639
I have to let people know too,

164
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:55,100
so no one else gets ideas about you.

165
00:08:56,879 --> 00:08:57,419
Right.

166
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,299
Wearing this,

167
00:09:00,220 --> 00:09:01,759
no one will dare get ideas about me.

168
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:04,259
It looks nice!

169
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:04,960
It looks good.

170
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:09,360
Looks good.

171
00:09:10,379 --> 00:09:11,600
You've got great taste.

172
00:09:16,919 --> 00:09:17,639
And this one.

173
00:09:18,399 --> 00:09:19,740
You bought quite a lot of stuff.

174
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,279
Are you taking all this back with you?

175
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,039
Yeah.

176
00:09:22,179 --> 00:09:23,259
Every time I go back to Shanghai,

177
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:25,500
this is how I let my parents know I'm doing well.

178
00:09:26,759 --> 00:09:28,240
Let's drop them off at the dorm first,

179
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,120
and then head to the bookstore.

180
00:09:29,340 --> 00:09:29,700
Sure.

181
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:30,700
Hop on.

182
00:09:32,279 --> 00:09:33,960
Let's catch a movie after the bookstore.

183
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,139
Sounds good. You got it.

184
00:09:37,639 --> 00:09:38,500
I think this scarf of yours...

185
00:09:38,519 --> 00:09:39,720
doesn't look as nice as the one I just put on you.

186
00:09:40,639 --> 00:09:42,100
Are you all right?

187
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:48,740
My first year, I didn't come to Songliao.

188
00:09:49,139 --> 00:09:50,700
It was to a place nearby,

189
00:09:50,899 --> 00:09:52,740
a little place called Panshan County.

190
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:54,320
I was totally clueless back then.

191
00:09:54,460 --> 00:09:56,039
I'd never even left Shanghai growing up.

192
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:58,759
When I left, my parents saw me off at the train.

193
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,139
We sang the whole way,

194
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:04,019
"Farewell, Huangpu River; onward to the northern frontier!"

195
00:10:04,259 --> 00:10:05,259
Was that the tune?

196
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:08,779
We rode the train for three days and three nights to get there.

197
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:11,100
At first, it all felt so new and exciting.

198
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,659
Then the female educated youth started crying.

199
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:14,259
Why?

200
00:10:14,379 --> 00:10:15,259
Homesick.

201
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:16,480
When they got tired of crying,

202
00:10:16,519 --> 00:10:17,799
the male educated youth started crying too.

203
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,299
When we finally got off the train and looked around,

204
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,440
we wondered, what kind of place is this?

205
00:10:22,039 --> 00:10:23,580
But our tears had already dried up,

206
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:24,799
and we were just numb.

207
00:10:26,799 --> 00:10:28,159
Panshan County...

208
00:10:28,399 --> 00:10:29,840
Never been there. What's it like?

209
00:10:31,279 --> 00:10:32,059
You wouldn't know.

210
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:34,879
We had a saying:

211
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:35,679
It went,

212
00:10:36,399 --> 00:10:38,019
"One street, one building,

213
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,960
one cop watching both ends.

214
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,799
One park, one monkey,

215
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:43,320
takes just a few minutes

216
00:10:43,559 --> 00:10:45,120
to walk from end to end."

217
00:10:45,899 --> 00:10:46,700
It was tiny.

218
00:10:47,419 --> 00:10:48,720
But we had to build it up.

219
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:50,360
My driving skills

220
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,360
were honed right there, practicing day and night.

221
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:54,539
Later, I was transferred to Songliao.

222
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:56,500
A big city is so much better,

223
00:10:56,799 --> 00:10:58,460
but it's still different from Shanghai.

224
00:10:59,179 --> 00:10:59,620
Look.

225
00:11:00,340 --> 00:11:01,080
Shanghai is here,

226
00:11:04,399 --> 00:11:05,460
and Songliao is...

227
00:11:06,279 --> 00:11:06,700
right here.

228
00:11:07,740 --> 00:11:08,620
That's pretty far.

229
00:11:13,299 --> 00:11:13,899
Haizhu,

230
00:11:14,559 --> 00:11:16,399
haven't you read *Gone with the Wind*?

231
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:17,700
Do you remember

232
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,019
Scarlett in it?

233
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,919
Buying up supplies everywhere.

234
00:11:21,220 --> 00:11:22,759
She said no matter what,

235
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,299
tomorrow is another day.

236
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,460
Didn't it feel like that when we were shopping just now?

237
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:28,139
Seeing all those people shopping,

238
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:30,299
everyone looked so resilient,

239
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:32,539
their faces beaming with hope for the future.

240
00:11:34,940 --> 00:11:36,559
I only heard about it on the radio.

241
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:38,820
That woman,

242
00:11:39,139 --> 00:11:41,460
wasn't she the spoiled daughter of a capitalist?

243
00:11:41,879 --> 00:11:42,620
She got denounced.

244
00:11:42,639 --> 00:11:44,559
Said she was a bloodsucker

245
00:11:44,639 --> 00:11:45,519
who exploited Black slaves

246
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:47,139
and pushed class oppression and stuff.

247
00:11:47,379 --> 00:11:48,879
In the end, didn't that man run off too?

248
00:11:49,019 --> 00:11:50,320
Didn't she bring it all on herself?

249
00:11:51,399 --> 00:11:52,940
Is that how you see it?

250
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:53,960
That's what they said.

251
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:57,419
Have you read this one?

252
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:58,860
*Anna Karenina*.

253
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:00,980
It's about a woman

254
00:12:01,279 --> 00:12:02,279
in that era,

255
00:12:02,899 --> 00:12:04,360
bravely pursuing love,

256
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:05,820
and in the end, throwing herself under a train.

257
00:12:06,799 --> 00:12:08,039
It's so tragic and moving.

258
00:12:09,059 --> 00:12:10,980
It's an indictment of that society.

259
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:16,059
I think I've heard of this one, too.

260
00:12:16,519 --> 00:12:17,340
Isn't it about

261
00:12:17,919 --> 00:12:19,679
that Russian woman's story?

262
00:12:19,759 --> 00:12:20,200
You know,

263
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:24,299
the one who had an affair, right?

264
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:32,759
But I think...

265
00:12:35,559 --> 00:12:36,399
this woman,

266
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:37,940
she didn't have it easy either.

267
00:12:38,379 --> 00:12:39,460
I mean, with New Year's coming,

268
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,240
everyone's out and about,

269
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:43,980
scrambling to buy some good food

270
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,220
or pick up some new fabric and stuff.

271
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,279
What's it all for?

272
00:12:47,679 --> 00:12:49,440
Isn't it just for a warm reunion,

273
00:12:49,639 --> 00:12:51,080
and a little comfort in their hearts?

274
00:12:53,259 --> 00:12:54,120
I figure

275
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:55,700
this woman...

276
00:12:56,259 --> 00:12:57,559
deep down in her heart,

277
00:12:58,399 --> 00:12:59,519
she hadn't warmed up yet.

278
00:13:01,039 --> 00:13:02,000
She never found someone

279
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:03,740
to share that reunion with.

280
00:13:04,460 --> 00:13:05,500
In this bitter cold,

281
00:13:05,940 --> 00:13:06,519
all on her own,

282
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,379
without any warmth in her heart...

283
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:10,799
It must've been so tough.

284
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,419
Want a roasted sweet potato?

285
00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:18,000
I'll buy you a roasted sweet potato in a bit.

286
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:24,200
You want one?

287
00:13:24,759 --> 00:13:25,279
Yeah.

288
00:13:25,279 --> 00:13:25,700
I do.

289
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:38,159
Um, Zhou Meng...

290
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:43,759
I actually have something I want to give you.

291
00:13:44,419 --> 00:13:45,019
What is it?

292
00:13:53,299 --> 00:13:53,840
Just a second.

293
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:57,360
I've had it ready for a while.

294
00:13:57,759 --> 00:13:58,159
Here... this...

295
00:13:58,159 --> 00:13:59,500
I just asked the bookstore,

296
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:00,519
and they said this

297
00:14:01,679 --> 00:14:02,220
is poetry.

298
00:14:13,299 --> 00:14:15,639
"Wishing Comrade Zhou Meng success at work."

299
00:14:16,679 --> 00:14:17,820
Why is it always the same line?

300
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:18,820
Can't you change it up?

301
00:14:20,039 --> 00:14:20,500
Well...

302
00:14:22,059 --> 00:14:23,159
There will be more later.

303
00:14:23,259 --> 00:14:24,159
I'll give you one every year.

304
00:14:24,919 --> 00:14:25,860
Next time. I'll change it next time.

305
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:29,399
No need.

306
00:14:30,559 --> 00:14:31,419
Just keep giving them to me like this.

307
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,360
I definitely will.

308
00:14:34,519 --> 00:14:36,100
I'm just not sure if the poem is good,

309
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:37,059
or if you like it.

310
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:38,299
If you don't like it,

311
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:39,120
I'll get you a different one.

312
00:14:44,879 --> 00:14:45,659
I like it.

313
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:55,799
Two tickets.

314
00:15:01,179 --> 00:15:01,580
Two tickets.

315
00:15:04,399 --> 00:15:04,740
Two tickets.

316
00:15:04,799 --> 00:15:05,500
All right, thank you.

317
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:09,759
All right, got them.

318
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:12,360
But it doesn't start for a while.

319
00:15:12,639 --> 00:15:13,740
Should we walk around a bit more?

320
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,139
Let's just sit here a bit.

321
00:15:17,519 --> 00:15:18,000
Sure.

322
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:19,480
Done eating?

323
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:20,419
I'll eat it later.

324
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:21,980
Let me wrap it up for you.

325
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:11,240
Over there!

326
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:15,559
Get lost!

327
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:18,660
You...

328
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:19,319
I didn't mean you!

329
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:20,279
Get lost! What're you looking at?

330
00:17:20,339 --> 00:17:20,859
Move!

331
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:21,420
Scram!

332
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:22,380
Move it!

333
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:25,460
Cripple Liu Haizhu first!

334
00:17:25,980 --> 00:17:27,480
Bring that girl back to me!

335
00:17:27,819 --> 00:17:28,480
Beat him up!

336
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:46,480
Let go of me!

337
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:48,319
Let me go! Stop it!

338
00:17:50,019 --> 00:17:50,660
Let go!

339
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,500
Don't grab me!

340
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:56,440
Get away!

341
00:17:59,660 --> 00:18:00,099
Run!

342
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:05,660
Go out the back and get the police!

343
00:18:05,819 --> 00:18:06,799
Haizhu!

344
00:18:25,019 --> 00:18:26,240
Hurry, go!

345
00:19:34,980 --> 00:19:35,700
Don't move!

346
00:19:37,619 --> 00:19:38,099
Let go!

347
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:41,900
The cops are here! The cops are here!

348
00:19:43,539 --> 00:19:43,980
Run!

349
00:19:44,279 --> 00:19:45,119
Quick! Go, go, go!

350
00:19:45,299 --> 00:19:45,839
Freeze!

351
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:47,059
Don't move!

352
00:19:47,339 --> 00:19:47,920
Haizhu!

353
00:19:48,319 --> 00:19:48,940
Haizhu!

354
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:50,740
Haizhu!

355
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:52,000
Haizhu!

356
00:19:53,579 --> 00:19:54,299
Are you okay?

357
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,579
Oh, Haizhu, Haizhu...

358
00:20:24,839 --> 00:20:26,380
Look at you, day in and day out.

359
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:29,259
All I hear is how you're running the turf again,

360
00:20:29,619 --> 00:20:30,980
how you took out the bad guys again,

361
00:20:31,599 --> 00:20:32,700
and how mighty you are.

362
00:20:34,099 --> 00:20:34,740
Let me tell you,

363
00:20:34,759 --> 00:20:35,599
no matter how mighty you are,

364
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:37,319
don't you still end up reporting here to me?

365
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:38,720
Get out.

366
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:42,180
Fine, I'll stop talking.

367
00:20:42,859 --> 00:20:43,779
Call me when the water's done boiling, okay?

368
00:20:58,259 --> 00:20:59,839
What's wrong?

369
00:21:02,819 --> 00:21:03,720
I'm fine.

370
00:21:04,720 --> 00:21:06,200
Don't listen to the doctor. He's making a big deal out of nothing.

371
00:21:06,339 --> 00:21:07,339
Even put this thing on me.

372
00:21:08,819 --> 00:21:10,059
I can walk, really.

373
00:21:10,380 --> 00:21:10,839
Trust me.

374
00:21:11,079 --> 00:21:12,579
Don't move. Lie down.

375
00:21:18,660 --> 00:21:19,920
You're in this state, and you're still acting tough.

376
00:21:23,319 --> 00:21:24,539
I'm not acting tough.

377
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:27,660
Look.

378
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:28,960
This time...

379
00:21:29,740 --> 00:21:31,200
I didn't even ask you to dress my wounds, did I?

380
00:21:38,039 --> 00:21:40,059
Hey, don't cry.

381
00:21:40,839 --> 00:21:42,019
I... I said the wrong thing.

382
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:44,640
I... I said the wrong thing.

383
00:21:44,779 --> 00:21:45,900
My bad, my bad.

384
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:48,859
I'm... I'm sorry.

385
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:49,740
I made you worry.

386
00:21:50,099 --> 00:21:52,359
D-Did I scare you?

387
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,059
Don't say you're sorry.

388
00:21:59,779 --> 00:22:00,819
It's not your fault.

389
00:22:01,220 --> 00:22:01,839
It's those guys.

390
00:22:02,500 --> 00:22:03,279
They were looking for trouble.

391
00:22:04,579 --> 00:22:05,980
They're real scumbags.

392
00:22:08,359 --> 00:22:09,339
I'm so useless.

393
00:22:11,319 --> 00:22:12,299
I'm gonna start training too.

394
00:22:13,019 --> 00:22:14,180
Next time something like this happens,

395
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:16,519
I can take a few hits for you.

396
00:22:17,599 --> 00:22:18,500
Train for what?

397
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:21,880
Don't you have me around?

398
00:22:22,940 --> 00:22:23,460
No, no.

399
00:22:23,700 --> 00:22:24,160
Well...

400
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:26,220
If I run into trouble again,

401
00:22:26,319 --> 00:22:27,460
I won't rush in headfirst anymore.

402
00:22:28,279 --> 00:22:29,480
We'll just steer clear.

403
00:22:29,819 --> 00:22:32,039
We'll leave the bad guys to the officers

404
00:22:32,099 --> 00:22:32,779
to deal with.

405
00:22:56,680 --> 00:22:58,220
You're absolutely right.

406
00:22:59,599 --> 00:23:01,880
All I want is for you to be safe.

407
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,579
I don't want to see you get hurt again.

408
00:23:05,799 --> 00:23:07,799
It was terrifying.

409
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:12,279
From now on, we don't need to make big money,

410
00:23:12,579 --> 00:23:14,079
or play the big hero.

411
00:23:14,319 --> 00:23:15,440
Just eat well,

412
00:23:15,539 --> 00:23:17,660
and work hard. That's enough.

413
00:23:20,039 --> 00:23:20,579
Okay.

414
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:22,519
I promise you.

415
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:25,880
We'll just live an honest life from now on,

416
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:27,539
and never cause trouble again.

417
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:32,180
I'm so useless.

418
00:23:32,319 --> 00:23:34,519
I couldn't do anything to help.

419
00:23:34,619 --> 00:23:36,579
I just had to watch you get beaten.

420
00:23:39,519 --> 00:23:41,500
There were so many of them,

421
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:44,099
all beating on you.

422
00:24:04,299 --> 00:24:05,940
How are they? Are they all right?

423
00:24:09,799 --> 00:24:11,200
Sun Biao, that scumbag!

424
00:24:11,980 --> 00:24:13,099
He couldn't beat us in a fair fight,

425
00:24:13,779 --> 00:24:14,460
so he played dirty!

426
00:24:15,380 --> 00:24:16,539
We can't just let this go.

427
00:24:16,579 --> 00:24:17,619
We have to avenge Zhu Zi!

428
00:24:17,619 --> 00:24:18,160
Keep it down.

429
00:24:22,380 --> 00:24:23,660
We just took his turf,

430
00:24:23,799 --> 00:24:25,099
and now he can still bring guys here.

431
00:24:25,299 --> 00:24:26,079
Something's fishy here.

432
00:24:27,700 --> 00:24:29,480
Zhang Haoran himself must have ordered this.

433
00:24:31,039 --> 00:24:31,779
We just got word.

434
00:24:32,539 --> 00:24:34,140
Zhang Haoran sent over a message.

435
00:24:34,839 --> 00:24:35,880
He wants to talk to you in private.

436
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:38,119
That bastard's up to no good.

437
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:40,920
Brother,

438
00:24:41,359 --> 00:24:41,880
why don't we just...

439
00:24:42,960 --> 00:24:44,339
make the first move and wipe them all out!

440
00:24:45,319 --> 00:24:46,900
There's no rush to settle the score right now.

441
00:24:49,259 --> 00:24:50,200
Don't you think

442
00:24:50,880 --> 00:24:52,059
the stunt Zhang Haoran is pulling

443
00:24:52,619 --> 00:24:54,279
seems awfully rushed and desperate?

444
00:24:57,019 --> 00:24:57,759
Tell the boys

445
00:24:58,259 --> 00:24:58,839
to stay sharp.

446
00:24:59,259 --> 00:25:00,119
The fox is coming out of its hole.

447
00:25:01,759 --> 00:25:02,819
What about Zhang Haoran?

448
00:25:03,299 --> 00:25:04,039
Are you seeing him or not?

449
00:25:07,740 --> 00:25:09,200
There can't be two kings on one mountain,

450
00:25:10,019 --> 00:25:11,559
let alone in this small corner of the underworld.

451
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:14,140
I'll see him.
